    "en": "Short answer (30–40 words)"
   },
   "problem": {
    "en": "Why is discovering that one's mind is one's own a sign of growing up?"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "A child usually accepts what parents and teachers say."
    },
    {
     "en": "The speaker realises he can think and decide for himself."
    },
    {
     "en": "Independent thinking is a mark of becoming an adult."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "A young child accepts what elders say. When the speaker realises that his mind is his own and he can use it as he chooses, he begins to think independently. This individuality is an important step out of childhood."
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us build a model answer together. Why is discovering that one's mind is one's own a sign of growing up?"
